Z||000000||Fleabitdog||12-19-2001||05:08 PM||||Anybody got any paypal stories they want to air? I have called them 5 times today to try to get $400 of my money. I need a lude!!!!<BR>It feels like it is thier money not mine. Story.... About 3 months ago there was an accident at work that involed me and a person dying because of a mistake I made. I have been off without pay .Fighting work/comp now.  As a result I have lost my checking account. Cancelled lack of funds.)<BR>Paypal will not let me have my money. I can't even transfer it to another persons account or get a check from paypal. I don't have credit cards and no funds to open new checking account so I cannot get reverified. They will not let unverified people send money yet a person sent me $160 last week and he was unverified. Does not make sense to me. Sorry to air my personal probs here but I needed to get it out. I don't want anyone to feel sorry for me. I have been through worse times and am still here. So no pity please. If anyone has any suggestions on what to do about paypal icould sure use some. Am tired from arguing with them. It seems like there are lots contradictions but they like to move around them.||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||12-19-2001||05:41 PM||||Get a family member that you trust to open a PayPal acct and accept a "payment" of your account balance and return cash to you.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Fleabitdog||12-19-2001||06:02 PM||||Thanks but if it was only that simple. They will not let me move the money anywhere. They won't even send me a check without getting verified. <BR>My roomate signed up for an account just to do that. No dice.... What gets me is they have you do all the verifying ( Name, email addy, street address, and bank) before they will even talk about your account on the phone and then they say you have to get verified (checking acct, or credit card) or we keep your money until you do. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-19-2001||08:01 PM||||There really only protecting you. What if someone else opened an account saying they were you and got your money. Just another reason in the present world you have to have a credit card, even if you never charge on it. Without one nowadays, you cant get a hotel room at some hotels, and renting a car with no card is nearly impossible. I once got caught out of town and forgot any cards, and couldnt get a rental car, I even offered to leave them $4,000 in cash I had with me. I let people pay me with paypal and just leave it in my account (it does draw interest) to buy stuff I want on EBay. That way I really never spend any money there, just add or subtract from paypal.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||12-19-2001||08:08 PM||||Does this $400 show up as a balance in your paypal account? If it does have someone put some ridiculous item on ebay for auction and you buy it for $400. Then you can have that $400 deducted from your account and sent to them, then they can pay you. I could do it for ya. I can put some little diecast car or something on, just charge you what they charge me for selling the 'item' Then send you a money order for it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||12-20-2001||06:58 AM||||Paypal are the pits. They rip me off big time on exchange rates. They are allways favouring themselves by about 4c in the dollar. Which can add up big time. Then they use the excuse to cover fluctuations.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"><BR>The rates don't fluctuate anywhere near their self imposed cut.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||8
